<!-- CONVERTED — VISUALLY VERIFIED --><chapter xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude" xml:id="ch15-sequences-and-infinite-series">
  <title>Sequences and Infinite Series</title>
  <shorttitle>Sequences and Series</shorttitle>

  <introduction><p>A sequence is an indexed list of numbers, and a series is defined by the limit of its finite partial sums. This chapter develops convergence criteria, tests for positive and signed series, and the distinction between absolute and conditional convergence. These results will justify the function series and approximations in the next chapter.</p></introduction>

